From d168c9a699187bf26aedf77877187c5c7fcc01e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 12:08:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: wait for GPU idle between tiles on A22X

With the a220 hardware binner enabled (W<=2/H=1 VSC config matching the
legacy KGSL capture), heavy scenes still wedge: hangcheck reports a "gpu
lockup" with the completed fence still slowly advancing, i.e. the 3D
back-end is stuck busy, not a hard hang.  This is the per-tile race the
force-sysmem investigation noted: fd2_emit_tile_renderprep reprograms
RB_COLOR_INFO, the window offset/scissor and VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID for the
next tile while the previous tile's draws and gmem2mem resolve are still
in flight -- there is no sync between tiles.

A plain OUT_WFI is known to be insufficient on A22X (see the pre-draw
VGT-DMA RBBM_STATUS poll workaround in fd2_draw.c), so reuse that same
CP_WAIT_REG_EQ RBBM_STATUS poll at the start of each tile's renderprep,
waiting for GUI_ACTIVE (bit 31) to clear so the previous tile has fully
drained before reprogramming.  Idle RBBM_STATUS reads 0x110; busy reads
0xc40103xx.

Upstream-Status: Pending [hardware workaround]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
index 03a967684c6..62c702c797d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a2xx/fd2_gmem.c
@@ -811,6 +811,28 @@ fd2_emit_tile_renderprep(struct fd_batch *batch,
    struct pipe_framebuffer_state *pfb = &batch->framebuffer;
    enum pipe_format format = pipe_surface_format(&pfb->cbufs[0]);
 
+   /* A22X: the hardware tile-binner is always active, and the per-tile
+    * state reprogramming below (RB_COLOR_INFO, window offset/scissor,
+    * VGT_CURRENT_BIN_ID, ...) races the previous tile's still-in-flight
+    * draw + gmem2mem-resolve pipeline -- there is no implicit sync between
+    * tiles.  On heavy scenes that race leaves the 3D back-end stuck busy
+    * (hangcheck "gpu lockup" with the fence still creeping), which the
+    * VSC pipe-config (W<=2/H=1, matching KGSL) alone does not fix.
+    *
+    * Wait for the GPU to go idle before reprogramming for this tile.  A
+    * plain OUT_WFI is not sufficient on A22X (see the pre-draw VGT-DMA
+    * workaround in fd2_draw.c), so reuse the same RBBM_STATUS register
+    * poll, here waiting for GUI_ACTIVE (bit 31) to clear -- i.e. the
+    * previous tile's draws and resolve have fully drained.  (Idle
+    * RBBM_STATUS reads 0x110; busy reads 0xc40103xx.) */
+   if (is_a22x(ctx->screen)) {
+      OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_WAIT_REG_EQ, 4);
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x000005d0); /* RBBM_STATUS */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000000); /* reference value: idle */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x80000000); /* mask: GUI_ACTIVE */
+      OUT_RING(ring, 0x00000001); /* poll interval */
+   }
+
    OUT_PKT3(ring, CP_SET_CONSTANT, 2);
    OUT_RING(ring, CP_REG(REG_A2XX_RB_COLOR_INFO));
    OUT_RING(ring, A2XX_RB_COLOR_INFO_SWAP(fmt2swap(format)) |
-- 
